# The generic tenant seed (#159): a runtime --role supplies the user and rig
# role. Agent identity belongs to rig/rig-templates, not this box release.
# KEY="value" only. Parsed against an allowlist, never sourced; there is no
# key for a network or a security flag, on purpose — the shared box-net
# profile is the placement contract and no template can weaken it.
# BOX_USER is a parser placeholder; cmd_new replaces it with --user or the
# runtime role-derived user before rendering cloud-init and stamping the box.
# /tmp is RAM and swap is provisioned, both in user-data.yaml and both
# deliberately DECOUPLED from the line below (#178): systemd sizes /tmp at
# 50% of BOX_MEMORY, so raising this figure raises the scratch ceiling with
# it and doubles the RAM scratch can eat — there is no value here that fixes
# that, only values that make it slower to notice. The seed therefore caps
# /tmp at a fixed 1GiB and lays a 4GiB swapfile on the disk; change either
# there, not here.
# The VM is this box's trust boundary: it runs untrusted agent code, so no
# silent container fallback when KVM is absent
# (BOX_NO_CONTAINER_FALLBACK, #175).
BOX_DESCRIPTION="Runtime tenant role on Debian 13 — box mints, rig converges"
BOX_IMAGE="images:debian/13/cloud"
BOX_USER="tenant"
BOX_CPU="2"
BOX_MEMORY="2GiB"
BOX_DISK="20GiB"
BOX_NO_CONTAINER_FALLBACK="1"
